/* 
You are given two non-empty linked lists representing two non-negative integers. 
The digits are stored in reverse order, and each of their nodes contains a single digit. 
Add the two numbers and return the sum as a linked list.

You may assume the two numbers do not contain any leading zero, except the number 0 itself.

*/

Create an empty linked list to store our answer.



Start with carry = 0 because we haven't added anything yet.



Look at the first number in each list.



Add the two numbers and the carry.



Write the last digit of the answer into our new linked list.



If the answer is 10 or more, keep the extra number as carry for the next addition.



Move to the next numbers in both lists.



Repeat steps 4–7 until both lists have no more numbers and carry is 0.



Return the new linked list.
